In my current game I tried out this wish, and it basically worked well.
The Archon never blinded me, only other creatures in the dungeon.  On
the other hand, it is supposed to be Lawful, but it seemed to attack
absolutely everything.  I'm playing an elf, but the temple on the
Gnomish mall level was lawful.  Since I didn't want to get any gods
angry at me by killing the priestess (that is what would happen if
I did kill her, right?), I waited around until Archie (the Archon)
walked in and killed her.  I then #offered her corpse at her own altar,
converting it to chaotic.  Then I had fun using up two wands of
create monster for offerings.  This showed another advantage of an
Archon as a pet: they don't eat.

Later on I took the portal to Fort Ludios (sp?), leaving Archie and
my other pets behind (more about them later).  Unfortunately, it
took me long enough to clear out the fort (I'm glad I was chaotic:
there must have been 100 gremlins there when I left, fortunately all
peaceful) that my pets were wild when I got back.  Archie attacked
me, and figured I would probably have to teleport away (according
to my stethescope he had 228 hp, ac -6), but I killed him with very little
trouble (level 13, 110 hp, ac -14, +3 Grimtooth, boots of speed, regen
ring, intrinsic telepathy).

One of my other pets was a Mind Flayer.  I had found a spellbook of
create familiar, which I had never seen before, so I tried it out,
which gave me a pet little dog.  Since I didn't see much point in
having a pet Archon and a pet little dog, I polymorphed the dog
(not the Archon :-), ending up with a Mind Flayer.  It seemed like
a decent pet (except that it nearly killed itself attacking a mindless
jelly with its tentacles).  However, I occasionally got messages about
it locking on to Archie, so I think it was actually making mental
attacks against him.  So in general I wouldn't suggest a Mind Flayer
as a second pet.
